00:26:10,923 --> 00:26:12,804
Approximately two hundred F.D.A.

524
00:26:12,804 --> 00:26:16,424
bureaucrats decide what eight billion people can try when dying.

525
00:26:16,984 --> 00:26:18,784
Here's the math on why that can't work:

526
00:26:19,304 --> 00:26:19,804
The F.D.A.

527
00:26:19,804 --> 00:26:22,344
approves approximately fifty new drugs per year.

528
00:26:22,784 --> 00:26:24,804
There are ten thousand known diseases.

529
00:26:25,344 --> 00:26:29,624
At that rate, covering every disease once takes two hundred years.

530
00:26:30,224 --> 00:26:33,404
And that's before you account for the fact that different patients respond

531
00:26:33,404 --> 00:26:38,244
differently to the same drug based on genetics, age, comorbidities, and

532
00:26:38,244 --> 00:26:39,104
whether they had breakfast.

533
00:26:39,764 --> 00:26:41,664
The real bottleneck isn't speed;

534
00:26:41,984 --> 00:26:42,824
it's information.

535
00:26:43,584 --> 00:26:47,064
Centralized approval assumes a two hundred-person committee can evaluate

536
00:26:47,064 --> 00:26:50,444
what works for eight billion genetically unique humans.

537
00:26:50,844 --> 00:26:51,644
They can't.

538
00:26:52,124 --> 00:26:56,824
A decentralized system where millions of patients generate real-world evidence

539
00:26:56,824 --> 00:27:02,344
simultaneously processes more therapeutic information in a month than the F.D.A.

540
00:27:02,344 --> 00:27:03,824
generates in a decade.

541
00:27:04,564 --> 00:27:05,204
The F.D.A.

542
00:27:05,204 --> 00:27:06,064
doesn't know:

543
00:27:06,064 --> 00:27:08,984
What disease YOU have (they haven't met you).

544
00:27:09,504 --> 00:27:11,344
How YOUR body responds to treatments

545
00:27:12,064 --> 00:27:12,864
(genetics are unique).

546
00:27:13,604 --> 00:27:18,484
What risks YOU'RE willing to take (some prefer death to side effects, others

547
00:27:18,704 --> 00:27:19,204
the reverse).

548
00:27:20,104 --> 00:27:25,264
Whether YOU'D rather die trying or die waiting (only you can answer this).

549
00:27:25,684 --> 00:27:27,644
But they decide for you anyway.

550
00:27:28,304 --> 00:27:29,344
This isn't ideology.

551
00:27:29,824 --> 00:27:31,144
It's information theory.

552
00:27:31,584 --> 00:27:36,164
You mathematically cannot centralize medical decisions for eight billion

553
00:27:36,164 --> 00:27:37,124
unique people.

554
00:27:37,684 --> 00:27:41,664
Every civilization I've worked with tried a centralized approval committee

555
00:27:41,664 --> 00:27:42,164
first.

556
00:27:42,704 --> 00:27:47,284
Every single one eventually abandoned it, once someone did the math and

557
00:27:47,284 --> 00:27:52,504
realized that a roomful of experts reviewing one drug at a time is just

558
00:27:52,504 --> 00:27:54,544
a queue with a death rate.

